{
  "name": "AKU-SONAM initiates think tank groups to advance nursing research",
  "parent_id": 203313789332670,
  "group_id": "36be6e46-bf09-41b2-b400-e7e9b97f2853",
  "alternates": [],
  "created_at": "2026-07-31T09:35:01.409Z",
  "deleted_at": null,
  "sort_by_date": null,
  "tag_list": [],
  "updated_at": "2026-08-12T15:04:59.507Z",
  "published_at": "2026-08-12T15:04:59.494Z",
  "id": 203984492210058,
  "uuid": "e237609b-9b2f-4678-bff8-114c0205d92b",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "6e52be08-41f1-9bba-2f85-b4c3aea5de73",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "ff8ecf1b-4df8-f7be-cf1c-11ae2c8e8723",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The event was conducted in collaboration between the Office of Research and Innovation and the Office of Graduate Programs at AKU-SONAM, in pursuit of one of the School's goals: to promote the development of a scientific body of knowledge that addresses needs of the local culture by generating context-based solutions. The main aim of this retreat was to identify faculty aspirations and needs, and help advance their contribution as researchers.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "One of the key highlights of the event was the official launch of five Think Tank groups within the School aimed to help expand AKU-SONAM's research portfolio and improve research outcomes as well as impact for local healthcare and patient-care solutions. These were categorized as follows:",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Day 1 was opened by Dr Tazeen Saeed Ali, professor and associate dean, research and innovation, AKU-SONAM. She shared the way-forward from Research Retreat 2018 and SONAM research milestones of the past four years. She also shared her research vision for the next two years which includes 100% faculty members becoming active researchers, increasing extramural fundings and publishing in high impact journals.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Dr Anjum Halai, Professor and Vice provost, AKU, shared expectations for faculty members in three main areas: teaching, research, and service. She further shared that faculty participation and expectation falls under the framework of 4 P's: Passion, Partnership, Purpose, and Publications.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Other speakers from the University included Dr Salim Virani, Vice Provost, Research; Dr Laila Akbarali, University Registrar; Dr Asad Ali, Dr Shehla Zaidi and Dr Kulsoom Ghias of the AKU Medical College; Dr Rozina Karmaliani, Dr Rafat Jan, Dr Rubina Barolia, Dr Laila Ladak, and Ms Shanaz Cassum, of AKU-SONAM, in addition to alumna Dr Zohra Lassi, Associate Professor, University of Adelaide. who joined virtually.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "A panel discussion held on Day 2 included speakers Dr Salim Virani, Vice Provost, Research, AKU; Ms Khairunnisa Hooda, Chief Nursing Officer, AKUH; and Dr Sarah Saleem, Professor and Section Head, AKU-CHS; moderated by Dr Tazeen Saeed Ali, Professor and Associate Dean of Research and Innovation at AKU-SONAM.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
